and structure and scoring potential. B4 has only one remaining tile, making it safer to discard.\nReason: Discarding B4 preserves the B2-B3 sequence and reduces risk of others needing it, while maintaining flexibility to form a Chow if B4 is drawn later. This supports forming four melds and a pair, which is a standard winning hand.\nAnswer: Play B4"}
